builderTools.panel.maskType.command = Command
builderTools.panel.maskType.command.description = Use mask commands to build a mask. The following symbols represent mask types:\n\
\n\
Above = >\nBelow = <\nNot = !\nAdjacent = ~\nNeighbor = ^\n\
\n\
Example: To mask grass blocks that are above dirt, you do:\n\
\n\
Soil_Grass,>Soil_Dirt
builderTools.panel.maskInvert = Invert\n\
\n\
Turns the current mask type into its opposite. For example, inverting a mask type of Above would make it search for blocks that aren't Above, which is equal to Below.
