builderTools.legend.ScriptedBrushPage.Title = Scriptable Brushes
builderTools.legend.ScriptedBrushPage.Description = This is a brush made in the Node Editor without any coding. If you want to make your own brush like this one, you can:
builderTools.legend.ScriptedBrushPage.ToolSettings = Open the creative tool settings.
builderTools.legend.ScriptedBrushPage.ExampleScriptedBrush.Title = Opening the Node Editor for Scripted Brushes:
builderTools.legend.ScriptedBrushPage.ExampleScriptedBrush.Description = 1. Go to Assets > Asset Node Editor.\n\
2. The Node Editor tool will pop up.\n\
3. In the Node Editor, click on Root Node: Demo Workspace and select Scriptable Brush. If asked if you want to continue, click OK.\n\
4. You are now in the Scriptable Brush workspace and can make a brush!
builderTools.legend.ScriptedBrushPage.NodeEditorBasics.Title = Scriptable Brush Node Editor Basics:
builderTools.legend.ScriptedBrushPage.NodeEditorBasics.Description = Now that you are in the workspace, you can make your brush by:\n\
- Using right-click to create a Node.\n\
- Using left-click on the bubble on the created Node and drag it to the bubble on the Root Node to connect it.
builderTools.legend.ScriptedBrushPage.NodeEditorSavingAndTesting.Title = Saving and Testing:
builderTools.legend.ScriptedBrushPage.NodeEditorSavingAndTesting.Description = 1. Go to File > Save or Save As, and save it to an Asset Pack.\n\
2. Go back to your game, and equip a Paint Brush Tool in your hand.\n\
3. Type in chat /sb load, and go to the brush you made.\n\
4. You can now start using your brush!
builderTools.legend.SelectTargetMaterial = Select targeted material
builderTools.legend.AddTargetMaterial = Add targeted material as multi-material
builderTools.legend.UndoLastBrush = Undo last brush action
builderTools.legend.RedoLastUndo = Redo last undone action
builderTools.legend.TipsAndTricks.Title = Tips and Tricks
builderTools.legend.TipsAndTricks.Description = Here are some tips and tricks for how to use this brush:
builderTools.legend.EditInventoryProperties = Edit the brush's settings from the inventory
builderTools.legend.SettingDescription = Below are descriptions of what each setting does for this brush:
builderTools.legend.BlockMasking = Block Masking
builderTools.legend.BlockMaskingDescription = Allows you to set materials to the brush that limit changes to blocks that match those materials.
builderTools.legend.BlockMaskingMenuDescription = To see all the masking options and what they do, you can:
builderTools.legend.BrushMenuMaskingTab = Open the Brush Settings
builderTools.legend.BlockMaskingMenuTabDescription = Open the Brush Masking Tab (near top right)
builderTools.legend.CreatingAndUsingMask = Saving/Delete Mask Presets:
builderTools.legend.CreatingAndUsingMask.Description = The "Save Mask" button allows you to save your mask as a preset to be used again.\n\
The "Delete Mask" button will delete the current mask preset you have loaded.
builderTools.legend.InvertingMask = Inverting a Mask:
builderTools.legend.InvertingMask.Description = The "Invert" button allows you to invert your current mask type to cover the opposite.\n\
\n\
For example, if the mask type is Above then it becomes Below.
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page1.Title = Paint Brush
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page1.Description = The Paint Brush Tool allows you to place and remove blocks in different shapes, sizes, and materials.
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page1.DestroyBlocks = Destroy blocks where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page1.PlaceBlocks = Place blocks where you're aiming, according to the material you've set
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page1.SelectTargetMaterial = Select targeted material
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page1.AddTargetMaterial = Add targeted material as multi-material
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page1.UndoLastBrush = Undo last brush action
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page1.RedoLastUndo = Redo last undone action
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page1.EditInventoryProperties = Edit materials, size, shape, and other properties from the inventory
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page1.AirPlacementTitle = Air Placement
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page1.AirPlacementHotkey = Toggle Air Placement targeting mode
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page1.AirPlacementDistanceChange = Change distance of air placement
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page2.AxisLock = Axis Lock
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page2.AxisLockDescription = Allows you to stick the brush to a flat, moveable, rotateable surface. The following hotkeys allow you to show, edit, and exit the surface mode.
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page2.ShowSurfaceMoveTool = Show Surface Move Tool
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page2.ShowSurfaceRotationTool = Show Surface Rotation Tool
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page2.UseBrush = Use Brush
builderTools.legend.PaintBrush.Page2.ExitAxisLockMode = Exit Axis Lock mode
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page1.Title = Cave Brush
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page1.Description = The Cave Brush Tool allows you to make caves and ravines.
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page1.DecorateArea = Add cave decorations where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page1.ShapeArea = Sculpt the cave area where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Title = Customizing a Cave:
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Description = You can customize what blocks the cave is made out of by dragging and dropping blocks from the inventory into the settings.\n\nYou can also remove blocks by double-clicking on blocks in the setting.
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page2.Example1.Title = Making and Decorating a Cave:
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page2.Example1.Description = 1. Look at the ground, the side of a mountain, or a solid chunk of land.\n\
2. Hold down the sculpt key, usually Right-Click, to start sculpting the shape of the cave.\n\
3. In the sculpted cave, look at the floor and hold down the decorate key, usually Left-Click, to add decorations.\n\
4. In the sculpted cave, look at the ceiling and hold down the decorate key, usually Left-Click, to add decorations.\n\
5. You now have a cave with decorations!
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page3.Title = Settings (1/2)
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page3.CaveBlocks.Title = Cave Blocks:
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page3.CaveBlocks.Description = - The blocks to make the cave out of.
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page3.CaveBlockDecorations.Title = Cave Block Decorations:
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page3.CaveBlockDecorations.Description = - The blocks to decorate the cave floor with on the sides of the Floor Blocks. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page3.TopDecorations.Title = Top Decorations:
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page3.TopDecorations.Description = - The blocks to decorate the cave ceiling with. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page3.FloorBlocks.Title = Floor Blocks:
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page3.FloorBlocks.Description = - The blocks to decorate the cave floor with. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page3.FloorDecorations.Title = Floor Decorations:
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page3.FloorDecorations.Description = - The blocks to place as decoration on top of the Floor Blocks. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page3.OreBlocks.Title = Ore Blocks:
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page3.OreBlocks.Description = - The ore blocks to place around the cave. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page4.Title = Settings (2/2)
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page4.Randomize.Title = Randomize:
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page4.Randomize.Description = - When checked, makes the shape smaller or larger at random when shaping the cave.
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page4.MeltStrength.Title = Melt Strength:
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page4.MeltStrength.Description = - Controls the carving strength of the brush. Higher = removes more blocks, Lower = removes fewer blocks.
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page4.SmoothStrength.Title = Smooth Strength:
builderTools.legend.CaveBrush.Page4.SmoothStrength.Description = - Controls the smoothing strength of the brush. Higher = more smooth, Lower = less smooth.
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page1.Title = Boulder Brush
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page1.Description = The Boulder Brush Tool allows you to make boulders and rock formations.
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page1.DecorateArea = Decorate the boulder where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page1.ShapeArea = Place a boulder where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Title = Customizing a Boulder:
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Description = You can customize what blocks the boulder is made out of by dragging and dropping blocks from the inventory into the settings.\n\nYou can also remove blocks by double-clicking on blocks in the setting.
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page2.Example1.Title = Making and Decorating a Boulder:
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page2.Example1.Description = 1. Look at the ground.\n\
2. Press the place key, usually Right-Click, to place a boulder.\n\
3. Change the Origin to Center.\n\
4. Look at the boulder and press the decorate key, usually Left-Click, to add decorations.\n\
5. You now have a boulder with decorations!
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page3.Title = Settings (1/2)
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page3.RockBlocks.Title = Rock Blocks:
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page3.RockBlocks.Description = - The blocks to make the boulder out of.
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page3.TopBlocks.Title = Top Blocks:
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page3.TopBlocks.Description = - The blocks to decorate the top of the boulder. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page3.TopDecor.Title = Top Decor:
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page3.TopDecor.Description = - The blocks to place on top of the Top Blocks. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page3.RockDecor.Title = Rock Decor:
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page3.RockDecor.Description = - The blocks to place on top of the Rock Blocks. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page3.BoulderPoints.Title = Boulder Points:
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page3.BoulderPoints.Description = - The number of sub-boulders to use to make the boulder. The sub-boulders can be spaced with Boulder Radius to make one boulder, or a group of boulders.
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page3.BoulderRadius.Title = Boulder Radius:
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page3.BoulderRadius.Description = - Controls the spacing between the Boulder Points. This can be used to make the boulder wider, or create a group of boulders.
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page4.Title = Settings (2/2)
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page4.Randomization.Title = Randomization:
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page4.Randomization.Description = - Controls how random the boulder looks. Higher = more random, Lower = less random.
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page4.Smoothness.Title = Smoothness:
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page4.Smoothness.Description = - Controls how smooth the boulder is. Higher = more smooth, Lower = less smooth.
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page4.StackSize.Title = Stack Size (Advanced):
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page4.StackSize.Description = - Controls how many times to stack the boulder using its Width. This is a different way to shape boulders. The boulder will place the current shape down, move it up by the Height, decrease the Width, and place again and keep doing this.
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page4.StackRandomization.Title = Stack Randomization (Advanced):
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page4.StackRandomization.Description = - The randomization between the height layers of the boulder. Higher = more random, Lower = less random.
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page4.StackTip.Title = Advanced Settings Tip:
builderTools.legend.BoulderBrush.Page4.StackTip.Description = - To see how the Stack Size and Stack Randomization work, turn Smoothness to 0, Shape to Cube, Stack Size to above 0, and try out different Width and Heights.
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page1.Title = Building Brush
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page1.Description = The Building Brush Tool allows you to make buildings and form structures.
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page1.ShapeArea = Place a building where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Title = Customizing a Building:
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Description = You can customize what blocks the building is made out of by dragging and dropping blocks from the inventory into the settings.\n\nYou can also remove blocks by double-clicking on blocks in the setting.
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page2.Example1.Title = Making a Tower with Windows:
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page2.Example1.Description = 1. Use the settings to make Width and Height to what you want.\n\
2. Change the Number of Floors to how many floors you want the tower to have.\n\
3. Change the Number of Windows to how many windows you want, and change the Window Radius so that the windows are placed properly in the wall. Windows take trial and error currently to get them placed properly in the wall.\n\
4. Change the Roof settings to be what you want.\n\
5. Press the place key, usually Right-Click, to place the building.\n\
6. You now have a tower!
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page3.Title = Settings
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page3.MainBlock.Title = Main Block:
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page3.MainBlock.Description = - The main blocks to make the building out of.
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page3.SecondaryBlock.Title = Secondary Block:
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page3.SecondaryBlock.Description = - The blocks used as decoration across the center of the walls of the building.
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page3.FloorBlock.Title = Floor Block:
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page3.FloorBlock.Description = - The blocks used for the floors in the building.
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page3.EnableWindows.Title = Enable Windows:
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page3.EnableWindows.Description = - Enables windows to be placed on the building.
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page3.WindowRadius.Title = Window Radius:
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page3.WindowRadius.Description = - The radius of where the windows should be placed. This setting may take playing around with to get it right.
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page3.EnableRoof.Title = Enable Roof:
builderTools.legend.BuildingBrush.Page3.EnableRoof.Description = - Enables the roof to be placed on the building. Turning off the roof is good for making walls.
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page1.Title = Decoration Brush
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page1.Description = The Decoration Brush Tool allows you to paint decoration.
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page1.DecorateArea = Clear blocks that match the blocks in Blocks to Clear.
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page1.ShapeArea = Paint the decorations where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Title = Customizing the Decorations:
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Description = You can customize what blocks are used for the decorations by dragging and dropping blocks from the inventory into the settings.\n\nYou can also remove blocks by double-clicking on blocks in the setting.
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page2.Example1.Title = Clearing an area and adding ground decorations:
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page2.Example1.Description = 1. Find an area you want to add decorations.\n\
2. Hold down the clearing key, usually Left-Click, to remove blocks from the area.\n\
3. Open the settings and add any decorations you want into the settings.\n\
4. Hold down the painting key, usually Right-Click, to paint the decorations on the area.\n\
5. You have now decorated the area!
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page3.Title = Settings
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page3.BlocksToClear.Title = Blocks to Clear:
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page3.BlocksToClear.Description = - The blocks to clear when using the clear blocks key, usually Left-Click.
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page3.FloorBlocks.Title = Floor Blocks:
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page3.FloorBlocks.Description = - The blocks to decorate with. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page3.DecorationBlocks.Title = Decoration Blocks:
builderTools.legend.DecorationBrush.Page3.DecorationBlocks.Description = - The blocks to place on top of Floor Blocks. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page1.Title = Forest Brush
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page1.Description = The Forest Brush Tool allows you to make forests and leafy brush.
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page1.DecorateArea = Add the selected decorations type where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page1.ShapeArea = Paints the ground where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Title = Customizing a Forest:
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Description = You can customize what blocks the forest is made out of by dragging and dropping blocks from the inventory into the settings.\n\nYou can also remove blocks by double-clicking on blocks in the setting.
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page2.Example1.Title = Making and Decorating a Forest:
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page2.Example1.Description = 1. Look at the area where you want to make the forest.\n\
2. Hold down the paint ground key, usually Right-Click, to start painting the forest floor.\n\
3. Add ground decorations by changing the type to Foliage, and adding the blocks you want to use for plants in the Foliage Blocks.\n\
4. Hold down the decorate key, usually Left-Click, to place the foliage decorations.\n\
5. Add trees by changing the type to Trees.\n\
6. Hold down the decorate key, usually Left-Click, to place the trees.\n\
7. You now have a forest!
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page3.Title = Settings
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page3.NumDecorations.Title = # of Decorations:
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page3.NumDecorations.Description = - The number of decorations to place. Only applies when the Decoration Types is set to Trees or Boulders.
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page3.DecorationSpacing.Title = Decoration Spacing:
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page3.DecorationSpacing.Description = - The spacing between decorations to be placed. Only applies when the Decoration Types is set to Trees or Boulders.
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page3.FloorBlocks.Title = Floor Blocks:
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page3.FloorBlocks.Description = - The blocks to decorate the forest floor with. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page3.FloorOutlineBlocks.Title = Floor Outline Blocks:
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page3.FloorOutlineBlocks.Description = - The blocks to decorate the outline of the forest floor with. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page3.FloorPatchBlocks.Title = Floor Patch Blocks:
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page3.FloorPatchBlocks.Description = - The blocks to place randomly throughout the forest floor for decoration. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page3.FoliageBlocks.Title = Foliage Blocks:
builderTools.legend.ForestBrush.Page3.FoliageBlocks.Description = - The blocks to use for foliage on the forest floor. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place. Only applies when the Decoration Types is set to Foliage.
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page1.Title = Mountain Brush
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page1.Description = The Mountain Brush Tool allows you to sculpt mountains and terrain.
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page1.ShapeArea = Sculpt a mountain where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Title = Customizing a Mountain:
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Description = You can customize what blocks the mountain is made out of by dragging and dropping blocks from the inventory into the settings.\n\nYou can also remove blocks by double-clicking on blocks in the setting.
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page2.Example1.Title = Making a Mountain:
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page2.Example1.Description = 1. Look at the ground.\n\
2. Customize the blocks to use for the mountain by placing blocks in the Layer settings.\n\
3. Hold down the sculpt key, usually Right-Click, to start sculpting the shape of the mountain.\n\
4. You now can sculpt mountains!
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page2.Example2.Title = Making a Valley:
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page2.Example2.Description = 1. Look at the ground.\n\
2. Change the Number of Points to 1, and Point Spacing to above 40.\n\
3. Hold down the sculpt key, usually Right-Click, to start sculpting. Notice that you now have 2 places where the terrain is being formed.\n\
4. Sculpt in a straight line moving up and down to build up a cliff on both sides.\n\
5. You now can sculpt a valley! This ability can also be used to make multiple mountains or details in the mountains at the same time.
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page3.Title = Settings
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page3.TopLayer.Title = Top Layer:
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page3.TopLayer.Description = - The blocks that will be on the top of the terrain.
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page3.MiddleLayer.Title = Middle Layer:
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page3.MiddleLayer.Description = - The blocks that will be in the middle of the terrain.
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page3.BottomLayer.Title = Bottom Layer:
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page3.BottomLayer.Description = - The blocks that will be on the bottom of the terrain.
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page3.NumberOfPoints.Title = Number of Points:
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page3.NumberOfPoints.Description = - The number of points to use to sculpt the mountains.
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page3.PointSpacing.Title = Point Spacing:
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page3.PointSpacing.Description = - The spacing between the Number of Points used to sculpt the mountain.
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page3.Smoothness.Title = Smoothness:
builderTools.legend.MountainBrush.Page3.Smoothness.Description = - Controls how smooth the sculpted terrain will be. Higher = more smooth, lower = less smooth.
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page1.Title = Path Brush
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page1.Description = The Path Brush Tool allows you to make paths.
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page1.DecorateArea = Adds half-blocks near level changes to make the path smoother
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page1.ShapeArea = Draw a path where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Title = Customizing a Path:
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Description = You can customize what blocks the path is made out of by dragging and dropping blocks from the inventory into the settings.\n\nYou can also remove blocks by double-clicking on blocks in the setting.
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page2.Example1.Title = Making a Path:
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page2.Example1.Description = 1. Look at the ground.\n\
2. Customize the blocks to use for the path by placing blocks in the settings.\n\
3. Hold down the draw key, usually Right-Click, to start drawing the path.\n\
4. Hold down the half-block key, usually Left-Click, to place down half-blocks near un-level areas to make them smoother.\n\
5. You now have a path with decorations!
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page3.Title = Settings
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page3.PathBlocks.Title = Path Blocks:
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page3.PathBlocks.Description = - The main blocks the path will be made out of. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page3.OutlineBlocks.Title = Outline Blocks:
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page3.OutlineBlocks.Description = - The blocks to place on the outline of the path. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place. Comes with a Width slider to control how wide it will be.
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page3.DecorationBlocks.Title = Decoration Blocks:
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page3.DecorationBlocks.Description = - The blocks to add as decorations along the path. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place. Comes with a Width slider to control how wide it will be.
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page3.HalfBlocks.Title = Half-Blocks on Path:
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page3.HalfBlocks.Description = - The half-blocks to be placed near un-level areas to make them smoother.
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page3.ClearObstacles.Title = Clear Obstacles:
builderTools.legend.PathBrush.Page3.ClearObstacles.Description = - If enabled, removes obstacles in the way of the path.
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page1.Title = River Brush
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page1.Description = The River Brush Tool allows you to make rivers and oceans.
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page1.DecorateArea = Adds decorations where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page1.ShapeArea = Draw a river where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Title = Customizing a River:
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Description = You can customize what blocks the river is made out of by dragging and dropping blocks from the inventory into the settings.\n\nYou can also remove blocks by double-clicking on blocks in the setting.
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page2.Example1.Title = Making a River/Waterfall:
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page2.Example1.Description = 1. Look at a surface.\n\
2. Customize the blocks to use for the river by placing blocks in the settings.\n\
3. Hold down the draw key, usually Right-Click, to start drawing the river.\n\
4. Hold down the decoration key, usually Left-Click, to place down decorations on the side of the river, under the water, and on top of the water.\n\
5. You now have a river and/or waterfall!
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page3.Title = Settings
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page3.FluidMaterial.Title = Fluid Material:
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page3.FluidMaterial.Description = - The fluid material the river will be made out of.
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page3.SurfaceBlocks.Title = Blocks above Fluid:
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page3.SurfaceBlocks.Description = - The blocks to place on the side and under the fluid of the river. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place. Comes with a Width slider to control how wide it will be.
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page3.SubsurfaceBlocks.Title = Blocks under Fluid:
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page3.SubsurfaceBlocks.Description = - The blocks to place under the fluid of the river. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page3.UnderDecorations.Title = Decorations under Fluid:
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page3.UnderDecorations.Description = - The decorations to add under the fluid. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page3.SideDecorations.Title = Decorations on side of Fluid:
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page3.SideDecorations.Description = - The decorations to add on the side of the river. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page3.TopDecorations.Title = Decorations on top of the Fluid:
builderTools.legend.RiverBrush.Page3.TopDecorations.Description = - The decorations to add on the top of the river. Comes with a Density slider to control how many to place.
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page1.Title = Spiral Brush
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page1.Description = The Spiral Brush Tool allows you to make spirals and circular patterns.
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page1.ShapeArea = Place a spiral where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Title = Customizing a Spiral:
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page2.BlockTip.Description = You can customize what blocks the spiral is made out of by dragging and dropping blocks from the inventory into the settings.\n\nYou can also remove blocks by double-clicking on blocks in the setting.
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page2.Example1.Title = Making a Custom Spiral:
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page2.Example1.Description = 1. Look at a surface.\n\
2. Customize the blocks to use for the spiral by placing blocks in the settings.\n\
3. Change the Number of Points to be what you need. Higher = more points in the spiral, Lower = less points in the spiral.\n\
4. Change the Radius to be 15. This will make it wide enough to see what the tool does.\n\
5. If you want a spiral going upward, change the Vertical Spacing to be higher than 0.\n\
6. Change which way the spiral is drawn by checking the Flip, Rotate Direction, or Invert Direction boxes.\n\
7. You can also add smoothing to the spiral by changing the Smoothness to be higher than 0.\n\
8. You can also choose to Hollow Center to make the center of the spiral made of air.\n\
9. You now have a spiral!
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.Title = Settings
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.NumberPoints.Title = Number of Points:
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.NumberPoints.Description = - The number of points on the spiral.
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.Radius.Title = Radius:
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.Radius.Description = - The radius of the spiral, which is how wide it will be.
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.VerticalSpacing.Title = Vertical Spacing:
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.VerticalSpacing.Description = - How far apart each point in the spiral is from each other, which is how tall it will be.
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.Flip.Title = Flip
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.Flip.Description = - Flips the order the spiral is drawn.
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.RotateDirection.Title = Rotate Direction
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.RotateDirection.Description = - Rotates the spiral 180 degrees.
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.InvertDirection.Title = Invert Direction
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.InvertDirection.Description = - Inverts the direction the spiral is drawn.
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.Smoothness.Title = Smoothness
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.Smoothness.Description = - Controls how smooth the spiral will be. Higher = more smooth, Lower = less smooth.
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.HollowCenter.Title = Hollow Center
builderTools.legend.SpiralBrush.Page3.HollowCenter.Description = - If enabled, replaces the center of the spiral with air from where you clicked.
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page1.Title = Revolve Tool
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page1.Description = The Revolve Tool allows you to rotate and paste a selection. This tool will only work if a selection has been made.
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page1.ShapeArea = Does the revolve. Depending on what settings you are using, it will do the revolve around where you are aiming, or yourself.
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page2.Example1.Title = Revolving with the Brush:
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page2.Example1.Description = 1. Make a selection that you want to have revolved.\n\
2. Equip the Revolve Tool.\n\
3. Set settings to what you want.\n\
4. Aim the brush to where you want the selection to be revolved around.\n\
5. Press the revolve key, usually Right-Click.\n\
6. You now have revolved your selection!
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page2.Example2.Title = Making a Full Circle around Yourself:
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page2.Example2.Description = 1. Make a selection that you want to have revolved.\n\
2. Equip the Revolve Tool.\n\
3. Set the Fully Revolve setting to checked, and change the Target to Player (Self).\n\
4. Move yourself so you are some blocks away from your selection.\n\
5. Press the revolve key, usually Right-Click.\n\
6. You now fully revolved the selection around yourself!
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page3.Title = Settings
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page3.Sampling.Title = Fill Strategy:
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page3.Sampling.Description = - The strategy to fill holes in the revolve. Revolving can sometimes leave holes, this will attempt to fill those holes.
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page3.FullyRevolve.Title = Fully Revolve:
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page3.FullyRevolve.Description = - Will revolve the selection entirely in a circle. This will ignore the Place Count and entirely revolve the selection.
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page3.PlaceCount.Title = Paste Count:
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page3.PlaceCount.Description = - Controls how many times to paste the selection in the revolve. For example, if this set to 5 then the selection will paste 5 times.
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page3.CenterAround.Title = Center Around:
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page3.CenterAround.Description = - Controls the target to revolve around. Brush Target = revolve around where the brush is aimed, Player (Self) = revolves around where you are.
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page3.UseCustomDistance.Title = Use Custom Radius:
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page3.UseCustomDistance.Description = - Pastes and revolves the selection where aimed, and uses Custom Radius to control the spacing from the center.
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page3.PlaceDistance.Title = Custom Radius:
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page3.PlaceDistance.Description = - The radius to control the spacing between the center and the revolve points. Higher = more wide, Lower = less wide.
builderTools.legend.RevolveTool.Page4.Title = Settings (2/2)
builderTools.legend.LineBrush.Page1.Title = Line Brush
builderTools.legend.LineBrush.Page1.Description = Allows you to build straight lines of blocks.
builderTools.legend.LineBrush.Page1.StartOrAddPoint = Start or add point to the line
builderTools.legend.LineBrush.Page1.CancelLine = Cancel Line
builderTools.legend.LineBrush.Page1.SnapToAngles = Hold to enable snapping to different 45° angles
builderTools.legend.LineBrush.Page1.EditInventoryProperties = Edit materials, size, and other properties from the inventory
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page1.Title = Getting Started
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page1.Description = Create keyframed animations using actors, cameras, particles, sounds, and more! Perfect for cinematics and cutscenes.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page1.OpensMenu = Open Machinima Editor UI
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page1.BaseCommand = Base command for all machinima operations
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page1.Scenes = Scenes\n\
A Scene is a container for your machinima. It stores all actors, keyframes, and settings.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page1.CreatingFirstScene = Creating your first Scene\n\
1. Find a nice spot for your machinima\n\
2. Open the Machinima Menu\n\
3. Click the + icon to create a new Scene\n\
4. Add your first Actor!
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page1.Actors = Actors\n\
An Actor is a keyframe-animatable object. See the next page for actor types.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page1.AddingCameraActor = Adding a Camera Actor\n\
1. Position yourself where you want the camera\n\
2. Open the Machinima Menu\n\
3. Click the + icon under the scene list\n\
4. Select "Camera" from the dropdown\n\
5. You can now click on the camera to reposition it, and press C to toggle the camera view!
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page2.Title = Actor Types
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page2.Description = Different actor types serve different purposes in your machinima. They're all animateable objects that allow you to control position, rotation, and other values. Actors are added via the Machinima Menu
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page2.CameraHeader = Camera
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page2.CameraDesc = Allows you to move a camera across paths and animate various settings such as FOV and Speed.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page2.EntityHeader = Entity
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page2.EntityDesc = Animated characters with models. Supports body/head rotation and animation events.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page2.PlayerHeader = Player
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page2.PlayerDesc = Similar to Entity, references the local player.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page2.ReferenceHeader = Reference
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page2.ReferenceDesc = Invisible marker points. Useful for targeting and reference positions. Allows you to set camera targets to track the points.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page2.ItemHeader = Item
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page2.ItemDesc = Displays items in the world. Can be positioned and animated.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page2.AddActorCommand = Command: .mach actor add [type] [name]\n\
Types: camera, entity, player, ref, item
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page3.Title = Playback Controls
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page3.Description = Playback controls let you preview your scene by animating all actors along their keyframe paths. Use these to scrub through time, jump between keyframes, and test your animations. Every frame will update all the actors along their keyframe paths, running the animations.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page3.TogglePause = Toggle Play / Pause
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page3.ContinuousPlayback = Toggle Continuous Playback (loops)
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page3.AutoRestart = Toggle Auto-Restart on scene end
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page3.RestartScene = Restart Scene from beginning
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page3.EndScene = Skip to final frame
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page3.NavigationTitle = Frame Navigation:
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page3.FrameScrub = Scrub through frames (hold for continuous)
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page3.JumpKeyframe = Jump to previous / next keyframe point
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page3.SpeedModifiers = Hold SHIFT for 2x speed, ALT for 0.5x speed
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page4.Title = Keyframe Editing
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page4.Description = Keyframes define an actor's position, rotation, and settings at specific points in time. The system interpolates between keyframes to create smooth animation paths. Add keyframes to create motion, edit them to fine-tune timing and positioning.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page4.AddKeyframe = Add new keyframe at the end of the actor's track, extending the animation
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page4.AddAtCurrentFrame = Insert a keyframe at the current playback position
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page4.CopyKeyframe = Copy selected keyframe settings to paste on another actor or frame
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page4.DeleteKeyframe = Remove the keyframe you're hovering over
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page4.EditKeyframe = Open gizmo to adjust keyframe position and rotation
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page4.MoveActor = Reposition the entire actor path as a whole
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page4.EditFrameTime = Change when this keyframe occurs in the timeline
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page4.AdjustFrameTime = Nudge keyframe timing earlier or later
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page5.Title = Mouse Interactions
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page5.Description = Click on keyframe nodes in the world to interact:
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page5.SelectKeyframe = Select keyframe (enter Free Move mode)
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page5.JumpToKeyframe = Set as active and jump to frame
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page5.GizmoTitle = Gizmo Controls:
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page5.TranslationGizmo = Open Translation Gizmo (axis-locked)
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page5.RotationGizmo = Open Rotation Gizmo (head/body)
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page5.FreeMoveTitle = Free Move Mode:
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page5.FreeMoveDescription = Left-click to confirm position, Right-click to cancel.\n\
Hold SHIFT to snap to surfaces at distance.\n\
Hold ALT to ignore surface snapping.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page6.Title = Selection Modes
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page6.Description = Selection modes determine what gets moved when you use transformation tools. Choose the right mode based on what you want to reposition.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page6.CycleMode = Cycle between selection modes
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page6.KeyframeModeTitle = Keyframe Mode (Default)
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page6.KeyframeModeDesc = Moves only the selected keyframe. Use this for precise adjustments to individual points along an actor's path without affecting other keyframes.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page6.ActorModeTitle = Actor Mode
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page6.ActorModeDesc = Moves all keyframes for the selected actor together. The entire path shifts as one unit, preserving the shape of the animation.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page6.SceneModeTitle = Scene Mode
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page6.SceneModeDesc = Moves the entire scene origin, shifting all actors and their paths together. Useful for relocating your whole machinima to a different area.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page7.Title = Display & Origin
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page7.DisplayTitle = Display Toggles:
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page7.ToggleDisplay = Toggle editor overlay display
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page7.TogglePathNodes = Toggle path node visibility
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page7.ToggleCamera = Toggle camera actor on/off
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page7.ToggleFrustum = Toggle camera frustum display
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page7.OriginTitle = Scene Origin Controls:
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page7.GoToOrigin = Teleport to scene origin
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page7.SetOrigin = Set scene origin to player position
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page7.OffsetToOrigin = Offset entire scene to player position
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page8.Title = Paths & Curves
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page8.Description = Choose how keyframes are interpolated:
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page8.LinearHeader = Linear (Default)
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page8.LinearDesc = Straight lines between keyframes. Simple and predictable movement.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page8.BezierHeader = Bezier
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page8.BezierDesc = Smooth curves with control handles you can drag to shape the path.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page8.SplineHeader = Spline
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page8.SplineDesc = Automatic smooth curves that pass through all keyframes.
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page8.BezierCommands = Path Commands:
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page8.EnableBezier = Enable bezier
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page8.SmoothBezier = Smooth handles
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page8.EnableSpline = Enable spline
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page9.Title = Console Commands
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page9.SceneCommands = Scene: .mach scene [load | copy | rename]
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page9.ActorCommands = Actor: .mach actor [list | add | remove | set | model | move | clone | rotate | scale | clear]
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page9.EventCommands = Events: .mach event [list | add | remove]\n\
Event types: animation, camera, command, particle, target
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page9.FileCommands = Files: .mach save | load | files | autosave [seconds]
builderTools.legend.MachinimaTool.Page9.UtilityCommands = Utility: .mach tool | speed [value] | align | restart
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page1.Title = Prefab Pasting Brush
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page1.Description = Allows you to rapidly paste prefabs as if using a brush. Supports most features of the Paintbrush.
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page1.LoadPrefabOrCopy = Load a prefab or copy a selection
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page1.UseSelectionContents = To use the contents of a selection, make a selection using the selection tool and type "/copy" then come back to the paste tool to use your copy
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page1.OpensPrefabList = Open the Prefab List; click a prefab to load
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page1.PastePrefab = Paste prefab; hold to brush prefab
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page1.StickPrefab = Attach the prefab to your target or detach if already attached
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page1.RotatePrefabY = Rotate around Y
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page1.RotatePrefabLookAxis = Rotate around look axis
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page1.FlipPrefab = Flip prefab along facing axis
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page1.CyclePreviewMode = Cycle preview mode (Blocks / Outline / Target)
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page1.CycleOrigin = Cycle origin (Bottom/Center/Top)
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page2.Title = Modifier Keys
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page2.ShiftPrefabLeftRight = Shift prefab left or right
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page2.ShiftPrefabForwardBackward = Shift prefab forward or backward
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page2.ShiftPrefabUp = Shift prefab up
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page2.ShiftPrefabDown = Shift prefab down
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page2.ResetShifting = Reset shifting
builderTools.legend.PasteTool.Page2.ResetRotation = Reset rotation
builderTools.legend.TintBrush.Page1.Title = Tint Brush
builderTools.legend.TintBrush.Page1.Description = Allows you to paint or blend tints on blocks.
builderTools.legend.TintBrush.Page1.BlendTints = Blend the tints where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.TintBrush.Page1.PaintTints = Paint your color where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.TintBrush.Page1.PickColor = Copy tint from target
builderTools.legend.TintBrush.Page1.UndoLastBrush = Undo last brush action
builderTools.legend.TintBrush.Page1.RedoLastUndo = Redo last undone action
builderTools.legend.TintBrush.Page1.EditInventoryProperties = Edit color, opacity, size, shape from the inventory
builderTools.legend.SculptBrush.Page1.Title = Sculpt Brush
builderTools.legend.SculptBrush.Page1.Description = Allows you to raise and lower the terrain to more accurately sculpt and blend shapes. Supports most features of the Paintbrush.
builderTools.legend.SculptBrush.Page1.MeltAwayBlocks = Melt away blocks where you are aiming, layer by layer
builderTools.legend.SculptBrush.Page1.RaiseLayer = Raise a layer of blocks where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.SculptBrush.Page1.Smooth = Smooth rough terrain
builderTools.legend.SculptBrush.Page1.MaterialSelectedDescription = When a material is selected, places a layer of that material where you're aiming
builderTools.legend.SculptBrush.Page1.SelectTargetMaterial = Select targeted material
builderTools.legend.SculptBrush.Page1.UndoLastBrush = Undo last brush action
builderTools.legend.SculptBrush.Page1.RedoLastUndo = Redo last undone action
