builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page1.Shrink = Shrink blocks - the red blocks.
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page1.Fill = Fills blocks by replacing air with material
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page2.ExtrudeTip.Title = Extruding
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page2.ExtrudeTip.Description = Extruding is expanding blocks outward in a direction. Length and Width control how much of the surface is extruded, and changing the depth will control how far it is extruded.\n\
\n\
If there are no materials in the block selector, it will extrude the blocks you are aiming at.
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page2.ShrinkTip.Title = Shrinking
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page2.ShrinkTip.Description = Shrinking is deleting blocks inward in a direction. Length and Width control how much of the surface is shrunk, and changing the depth will control how far it is shrunk.
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page2.FillTip.Title = Filling
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page2.FillTip.Description = Filling is replacing empty blocks in the tool area with a material. If the area you are filling is larger than the bounds of the fill area, it will stay within the bounds of that area.
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.Title = Advanced Settings
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.FilterTip.Title = Filters
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.FilterTip.Description = Below are the different filters for extruding/shrinking:
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.FilterAll.Title = All:
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.FilterAll.Description = - Uses all blocks.
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.FilterMaterial.Title = Same Material:
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.FilterMaterial.Description = - Uses only blocks that have the same material as the block being looked at.
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.FilterShape.Title = Same Shape:
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.FilterShape.Description = - Uses only blocks that have the same shape as the block being looked at.
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.FilterFullBlocks.Title = Full Blocks:
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.FilterFullBlocks.Description = - Uses only blocks that are full solid blocks. This excludes blocks like Leaves and other shrubbery.
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.FilterNotFullBlocks.Title = Not Full Blocks:
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.FilterNotFullBlocks.Description = - Uses only blocks that are NOT full solid blocks. This only includes blocks like Leaves and other shrubbery.
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.StrategyTip.Title = Strategy
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.StrategyTip.Description = Below are the different strategies for extruding/shrinking:
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.StrategyDefault.Title = Default:
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.StrategyDefault.Description = - The area affected will only include blocks touching air.
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.StrategyAll.Title = All:
builderTools.legend.Extrude.Page3.StrategyAll.Description = - The area affected will include all blocks, even blocks that cannot be seen on the surface (underground).
builderTools.legend.Color.Page1.Title = Color Tool
builderTools.legend.Color.Page1.Description = Color or Re-color blocks in an area using various coloring styles.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page1.CycleMode = Cycle between modes
builderTools.legend.Color.Page1.NextShape = Next shape
builderTools.legend.Color.Page1.PrevShape = Previous shape
builderTools.legend.Color.Page1.ColoringMode.Title = Coloring Mode:
builderTools.legend.Color.Page1.ColoringMode.Description = Replaces blocks with ones you choose, or finds the closest matching color blocks to use.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page1.GradientMode.Title = Gradient Mode:
builderTools.legend.Color.Page1.GradientMode.Description = Paint a gradient onto a surface using different shapes and blending.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page1.ShadingMode.Title = Shading Mode:
builderTools.legend.Color.Page1.ShadingMode.Description = Paint a surface with realistic coloring based on light and angles of surrounding blocks.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page2.GradientModeTip.Title = Gradient Mode
builderTools.legend.Color.Page2.GradientModeTip.Description = Allows you to paint many colors at a time to create a gradient.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page2.GradientModeTip.PaintArea = Click and drag to create the reference area to control the gradient.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page2.GradientModeTip.Paint = Paint the colors onto the area.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page2.GradientModeTip.ResetGuidingLine = Reset the Gradient Line.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page2.GradientModeTip.HowToUse.Title = Controlling the painting area:
builderTools.legend.Color.Page2.GradientModeTip.HowToUse.Description = 1. Click and drag to create the area to paint.\n2. Click and drag on the red and green boxes to extend the area to paint.\n3. Click and drag on the white boxes to control how much area a color will cover.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page2.GradientModeTip.Blend.Title = Blend:
builderTools.legend.Color.Page2.GradientModeTip.Blend.Description = The blend controls how much the colors will gradually blend into each other.\n\nLow blend = Colors won't be mixed together.\nHigh blend = Colors will be mixed together.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page3.ShadingModeTip.Title = Shading Mode
builderTools.legend.Color.Page3.ShadingModeTip.Description = Allows you to paint an area based on light/darkness and surrounding blocks.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page3.ShadingModeTip.Manual.Title = Manual
builderTools.legend.Color.Page3.ShadingModeTip.Manual.Description = Left-click to lighten the area, Right-click to darken the area.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page3.ShadingModeTip.Auto.Title = Auto
builderTools.legend.Color.Page3.ShadingModeTip.Auto.Description = Automatically shade the area using nearby blocks with both light and dark.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page3.ShadingModeTip.Custom.Title = Custom
builderTools.legend.Color.Page3.ShadingModeTip.Custom.Description = Customize what blocks to use for the shading, blocks added first are the lightest, and blocks added last are darkest.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page3.ShadingModeTip.Settings.Title = Settings
builderTools.legend.Color.Page3.ShadingModeTip.Settings.Description = Shading depends heavily on the settings you choose to achieve what you want. See next page for more information on settings.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page4.ShadingModeTip.LightSource.Title = Light Source
builderTools.legend.Color.Page4.ShadingModeTip.LightSource.Description = Controls the light source to use for shading.\n\nPlayer = Color is brightest the closer you are to the clicked area.\nBrush Center = Color is brightest the closer the block is to the brush center.\nSun = Color is brightest by contact with the sky.\nAngle = Color is brightest based on it's slope. Flatter = brighter, Steeper = darker.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page4.ShadingModeTip.Intensity.Title = Intensity
builderTools.legend.Color.Page4.ShadingModeTip.Intensity.Description = Controls the intensity of the shading.\n\nLower = less detail.\nHigher = more detail.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page4.ShadingModeTip.EdgeBlend.Title = Edge Blend
builderTools.legend.Color.Page4.ShadingModeTip.EdgeBlend.Description = Controls the amount of blending done around the edges of the brush.\n\nLower = less blending at the edge.\nHigher = more blending at the edge.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page5.ColoringModeTip.Title = Coloring Mode
builderTools.legend.Color.Page5.ColoringModeTip.Description = Allows you to quickly replace all the blocks that are the same as the one you are looking at.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page5.ColoringModeTip.Normal.Title = Normal
builderTools.legend.Color.Page5.ColoringModeTip.Normal.Description = Replace a single type of block with another type of block or blocks.
builderTools.legend.Color.Page5.ColoringModeTip.Auto.Title = Smart Match
builderTools.legend.Color.Page5.ColoringModeTip.Auto.Description = Replace a block based on it's type, and if no type is found, then use a block that is similar in color that does have the same type.
builderTools.legend.Palette.Page1.Title = Palette Tool
builderTools.legend.Palette.Page1.Description = Create, delete, and edit block palettes.
builderTools.legend.Palette.Page1.OpenPaletteEditor = Opens the Palette Editor
builderTools.legend.Palette.Page1.PaletteEditor.Title = Palette Editor
builderTools.legend.Palette.Page1.PaletteEditor.Description = The Palette Editor has several tools to allow you to create your own block palettes to be used while building.\n\
\n\
A palette is created by dragging and dropping blocks into the Palette's section towards the bottom. You can save your palette to be re-used as you please, and also delete palettes you no longer use.\n\
\n\
More info on the Palette Editor is on the next page.
builderTools.legend.Palette.Page1.PaletteSettings = View your saved Palettes.
builderTools.legend.Palette.Page1.Usage.Title = Using a saved Palette
builderTools.legend.Palette.Page1.Usage.Description = Palettes that are saved can be re-used. You can load them into your hotbar, edit, save, and delete them.
builderTools.legend.Palette.Page2.Title = Palette Editor
builderTools.legend.Palette.Page2.Description = Allows you to edit palettes using color based tools.
builderTools.legend.Palette.Page2.BlockPicker.Title = Color/Block Picker
builderTools.legend.Palette.Page2.BlockPicker.Description = The Color Picker at the top suggests blocks that are similar in color to what you choose.\n\
\n\
You can also give it a block to have it try and find other blocks that have a similar color.
builderTools.legend.Palette.Page2.Gradient.Title = Gradient
builderTools.legend.Palette.Page2.Gradient.Description = The Gradient section in the middle gives you the ability to input blocks to find similar blocks between them to create smooth color transitions.\n\
\n\
Typically, putting a block on the far left and right in the slots give the fullest gradient between the two.
builderTools.legend.BlockSpawner.Page1.Title = Block Spawner
builderTools.legend.BlockSpawner.Page1.Description = Place in a prefab to configure a block to spawn at that location with loot drops.
builderTools.legend.BlockSpawner.Page1.Interact = Opens the menu to configure the block spawner.
builderTools.legend.BlockSpawner.Page1.Configuring.Title = Configuring
builderTools.legend.BlockSpawner.Page1.Configuring.Description = The Block Spawner Asset dropdown allows you to select which BlockSpawnerTable asset to use for the block.
builderTools.legend.BlockSpawner.Page1.Editing.Title = Editing / Viewing Assets
builderTools.legend.BlockSpawner.Page1.Editing.Description = The Edit / Create Block Spawner Asset button takes you to a new menu that allows you to work with BlockSpawnerTable assets.\n\nYou can select an existing asset from the dropdown, or start adding entries to create a new one. Each asset contains entries that have the following:\n\nBlock Type = Container block to spawn.\n\nWeight = Weight for an entry between 0 - 1. The closer to 1, the more likely it will be used.\n\nDroplist = The drop asset to use to allow items to spawn in the block.
builderTools.legend.BlockSpawner.Page1.AssetEditor.Title = Asset Editor
builderTools.legend.BlockSpawner.Page1.AssetEditor.Description = The Asset Editor, which is accessed in the Creative Tools, can be used to further configure BlockSpawnerTable or Drop assets.
